# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# Deny everything at the root, then re-include only what the two builds need.
# Nothing else reaches the build context, so local credential files (local_*),
# kubeconfigs and notes cannot end up in an image by accident.
#
# NOTE: this uses `*` plus directory re-includes, deliberately NOT `**` plus
# `!**/*.go`. The legacy docker builder (no BuildKit) does not re-include files
# that sit under an excluded directory, so the `**` form yields a context of
# only go.mod/go.sum and the build fails with
# "package cmd/main.go is not in std". BuildKit accepts both forms.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!api
!cmd
!internal
!proto

# Tests never belong in a release image.
**/*_test.go
